  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-01",
      "unit": [
        "007_BerryPlant.rb",
        1,
        45
      ],
      "fact": "DATA empty; DATA_FILENAME berry_plants.dat; PBS_BASE_FILENAME berry_plants. SCHEMA SectionName→id m symbol (word characters, first not digit), HoursPerStage→hours_per_stage v positive integer, DryingPerHour→drying_per_hour u nonnegative integer, Yield→yield uv exactly the first two schema fields parsed as nonnegative and positive. get_csv_record does not reject surplus CSV fields after the nonrepeating schema; absent required parsed fields fail cast. These schema constraints apply to compiler parsing, not direct constructor validation."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-02",
      "unit": [
        "007_BerryPlant.rb",
        28,
        43
      ],
      "fact": "Constructor id is direct supplied hash value. false/nil hours/drying/yield/suffix fall back through || to 3/15/[2,5]/empty string; zero is retained. If yield[1]<yield[0], reverse! mutates the very supplied yield array; no clone, length/type/range validation. minimum_yield and maximum_yield are direct indices0/1. Missing properties within a registered parsed record use defaults; an absent whole ID has no automatic default record."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-03",
      "unit": [
        "007_BerryPlant.rb",
        20,
        23
      ],
      "fact": "NUMBER_OF_REPLANTS=9, NUMBER_OF_GROWTH_STAGES=4, NUMBER_OF_FULLY_GROWN_STAGES=4; WATERING_CANS ordered SPRAYDUCK,SQUIRTBOTTLE,WAILMERPAIL,SPRINKLOTAD. Declaration does not prove inventory/native image availability."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-04",
      "unit": [
        "001_GameData.rb",
        78,
        151
      ],
      "fact": "Symbol class methods accept Symbol, same class object, String; String converts to_sym. get returns supplied same-class instance directly; absent keyed ID raises Unknown ID, try_get nil or absent ID returns nil, exists?(nil) false. register stores new constructor at hash[:id] without its own duplicate check. each is DATA.each_value order. save writes Data/berry_plants.dat through save_data; load replaces DATA via load_data, does not reconstruct each object using constructor."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-05",
      "unit": [
        "001_Compiler.rb",
        967,
        1003
      ],
      "fact": "Default discovery chdir PBS then Dir.glob *.txt only, matches exact berry_plants base or berry_plants_ prefix. It does not recursively include Gen 5/6/7/8 backup subdirectories and does not select PBS backup by MECHANICS_GENERATION. compile_pbs_files calls berry compilation after items; explicit compile_berry_plants(*paths) can choose alternate paths. Thus these Gen5 records are alternate corpus, not current default by generation. Other backup path equal blobs are not this reader FULL_READ."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-06",
      "unit": [
        "002_Compiler_CompilePBS.rb",
        4,
        66
      ],
      "fact": "BerryPlant has no OPTIONAL constant. Generic compile clears DATA before path processing; computes suffix from basename; reads schema-listed properties and leaves missing properties absent; calls empty validate_compiled_berry_plant; rejects duplicate ID before register; registers each completed record; after all files calls empty validate_all_compiled_berry_plants then saves. Parse/duplicate/register/Graphics/message/file failure preserves actual in-memory prefix after clear and prior records. Save is not reached on earlier failure; no transaction/rollback or guaranteed restored prior DATA. No berry Item-existence validation in these empty validation methods."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-07",
      "unit": [
        "003_Compiler_WritePBS.rb",
        4,
        64
      ],
      "fact": "write_berry_plants delegates generic writer. Paths are generated from current records unique pbs_file_suffix, not backup discovery; empty suffix→PBS/berry_plants.txt, nonempty→PBS/berry_plants_suffix.txt. Each opens wb, writes BOM and localized header, then matching records in each order, schema properties through get_property_for_PBS and pbWriteCsvRecord. Generic property getter returns false/empty array as nil, other values retained. Mid-write failure can leave truncated/partial current file and previously completed files; no temp/rename/rollback. Empty DATA gives no paths and no output. Writer does not choose Gen5 backup automatically."
    },
    {
      "id": "BERRY-KER-08",
      "fact": "All 64 shared IDs have exactly equal HoursPerStage,DryingPerHour,Yield in default and Gen5 corpus. Default adds ROSELIBERRY (18,6,[1,5]), KEEBERRY (24,7,[1,5]), MARANGABERRY (24,7,[1,5]); Gen5 lacks them. Missing whole-record queries follow get/try_get semantics above, not constructor defaults."
    }
  ],
